From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kern0x1b <kern0x1b@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] JavaScriptCore: carry the 32-bit JSValue and this device's
 runtime tuning

Upstream deleted the 32-bit JSValue representation. This restores it across
the runtime, heap, bytecode, interpreter, parser and API: the JSValue switch
and its conditional chains, array slots cleared the 32-bit way when a length
shrinks, the async generator resume value, map iteration's slow path called as
declared, and both halves of a double printed when dumping. It also builds with
assertions on ARMv7 and against trunk's WTF string and base64 interfaces.

The collector is tuned for a phone that jetsams at 282 MB: the absolute band,
the growth fraction and the code deletion threshold, and the inline caches a
32-bit build was forcing to fail.
